==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}
[[File:Operation_Castle_-_Romeo_001.jpg|thumb|125px|A [[w:nuclear holocaust|nuclear holocaust]] is sometimes associated with modern visualizations of [[w:Armageddon|Armageddon]]]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|he|en}} {{l/he|הר מגידו|dwv=‎הַר‎ מְגִדּוֹ|tr=har megiddo}}, used in [http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Bible_%28World_English%29/Revelation#Chapter_16 Revelation 16:16], referring to [[w:Tel Megiddo|Mount Megiddo]], the place of the last battle at the [[w:Last Judgment|Last Judgment]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɛdən|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|Ar|ma|ged|don|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|Christianity|Islam}} The site of a [[prophesied]] final battle between the forces of [[good]] and [[evil]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} The battle itself.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|Apocalypse}}, {{l|en|Final Judgment}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|en|Ragnarok}} {{gloss|Norse mythology}}
* {{l|en|day of reckoning}}, {{l|en|doomsday}}, {{l|en|judgement day}}, {{l|en|end times}}, {{l|en|end of the world}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse}}

